{"id":"CVE-2023-0361","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2023-02-15T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-14T19:28:14.889Z","description":"A timing side-channel in the handling of RSA ClientKeyExchange messages was discovered in GnuTLS. This side-channel can be sufficient to recover the key encrypted in the RSA ciphertext across a network in a Bleichenbacher style attack. To achieve a successful decryption the attacker would need to send a large amount of specially crafted messages to the vulnerable server. By recovering the secret from the ClientKeyExchange message, the attacker would be able to decrypt the application data exchanged over that connection.","cwe":["side-channel","CWE-203 CWE-203 Observable Discrepancy"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.4,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"gnutls","versions":["affected gnutls-3.7.6"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-0361"},{"url":"https://github.com/tlsfuzzer/tlsfuzzer/pull/679"},{"url":"https://gitlab.com/gnutls/gnutls/-/issues/1050"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/02/msg00015.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20230218 [SECURITY] [DLA 3321-1] gnutls28 security update"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/UFIA3X4IZ3CW7SRQ2UHNHNPMRIAWF2FI/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2023-1c4a6a47ae"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/Z634YBXAJ5VLDI62IOPBVP5K6YFHAWCY/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2023-5b378b82b3"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/WS4KVDOG6QTALWHC2QE4Y7VPDRMLTRWQ/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2023-4fc4c33f2b"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230324-0005/"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230725-0005/"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-398330.html"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-806742.html"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2023-3724","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"wolfSSL","published":"2023-07-17T21:13:10.623Z","updated":"2024-10-29T15:53:43.066Z","title":"TLS 1.3 client issue handling malicious server when not including a KSE and PSK extension","description":"If a TLS 1.3 client gets neither a PSK (pre shared key) extension nor a KSE (key share extension) when connecting to a malicious server, a default predictable buffer gets used for the IKM (Input Keying Material) value when generating the session master secret. Using a potentially known IKM value when generating the session master secret key compromises the key generated, allowing an eavesdropper to reconstruct it and potentially allowing access to or meddling with message contents in the session. This issue does not affect client validation of connected servers, nor expose private key information, but could result in an insecure TLS 1.3 session when not controlling both sides of the connection. wolfSSL recommends that TLS 1.3 client side users update the version of wolfSSL used. \n\n\n","cwe":["CWE-20 CWE-20 Improper Input Validation"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":9.1,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"wolfSSL","product":"wolfSSL","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 3.14.0 <=5.6.0 (release bundle)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/pull/6412","tags":["patch"],"name":"github"},{"url":"https://www.wolfssl.com/docs/security-vulnerabilities/","name":"website"}],"solutions":["\nFixed in the following GitHub pull request  https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/pull/6412 https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/pull/6412 \n\n\n"],"credits":[" Johannes from Sectra Communications and Linköping University"],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2023-4421","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mozilla","published":"2023-12-12T17:02:08.801Z","updated":"2025-11-04T19:25:18.220Z","description":"The NSS code used for checking PKCS#1 v1.5 was leaking information useful in mounting Bleichenbacher-like attacks. Both the overall correctness of the padding as well as the length of the encrypted message was leaking through timing side-channel. By sending large number of attacker-selected ciphertexts, the attacker would be able to decrypt a previously intercepted PKCS#1 v1.5 ciphertext (for example, to decrypt a TLS session that used RSA key exchange), or forge a signature using the victim's key. The issue was fixed by implementing the implicit rejection algorithm, in which the NSS returns a deterministic random message in case invalid padding is detected, as proposed in the Marvin Attack paper. This vulnerability affects NSS < 3.61.","cwe":["Timing side-channel in PKCS#1 v1.5 decryption depadding code"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Mozilla","product":"NSS","versions":["affected unspecified <3.61 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1651411"},{"url":"https://www.mozilla.org/security/advisories/mfsa2023-53/"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/10/msg00039.html"}],"credits":["Hubert Kario"],"vendors":["crypto-libs","mozilla"]}
{"id":"CVE-2023-5981","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2023-11-28T11:49:50.138Z","updated":"2026-11-05T11:36:28.776Z","title":"Gnutls: timing side-channel in the rsa-psk authentication","description":"A vulnerability was found that the response times to malformed ciphertexts in RSA-PSK ClientKeyExchange differ from response times of ciphertexts with correct PKCS#1 v1.5 padding.","cwe":["CWE-208 Observable Timing Discrepancy"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"Red Hat severity rating","content":"{\"value\": \"Moderate\", \"namespace\": \"https://access.redhat.com/security/updates/classification/\"}"},{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","packageName":"gnutls","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:3.6.16-8.el8_9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","packageName":"gnutls","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:3.6.16-8.el8_9 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.6 Extended Update Support","packageName":"gnutls","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":["cpe:/a:redhat:rhel_eus:8.6::appstream","cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_eus:8.6::baseos"],"versions":["unaffected 0:3.6.16-5.el8_6.2 <* (rpm)"]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.8 Extended Update Support","packageName":"gnutls","collectionURL":"https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","defaultStatus":"affected","cpes":